/-
The WAL tester (`examples/etcd/wal`, the part `WalTester/`; `notes/wal-fsext-w4c-plan.md`, W4c U5),
every proof instantiated with its callees' results: the tester's own, and the WAL's and `durable`'s
linked results (their `Link.lean`s, used as they are). The callees are read off each proof's binders
(`etc/link_walfs.py`'s docstring); a binder `∀ W : WalGS GF, S (W := W) ...` (the WAL's specs at
every generation's ghost names) is given `fun W => ...`, and a hypothesis of the WAL's result that
mentions `W` becomes `∀ W : WalGS GF, ...`. Generated by `etc/gen-link.py --wal-tester` -- do not
edit by hand.

110 results, 97 of them with no hypothesis. The others take, as hypotheses `h_<name>`, the specs
with no proof and the premises on the model parameters (the client's protobuf laws, ...) they reach:
`h_U_Ok` (5), `h_U_SnapCoh` (5), `h_WalDecEnvSupply` (5), `h_WalHsOwn` (5), `h_WalHsOwn_2` (5),
`h_WalPbIn_CloneHsLaw` (5), `h_WalPbIn_GetIndexLaw` (11), `h_WalPbIn_GetTermLaw` (5),
`h_WalPbIn_IsEmptyLaw` (11), `h_WalPbIn_MarshalEntLaw` (9), `h_WalPbIn_MarshalHsLaw` (11),
`h_WalPbIn_MustSyncLaw` (9), `h_WalPbIn_NilLaw` (2), `h_WalPbIn_SizeLaw` (9),
`h_WalPbIn_UnmarshalEntLaw` (5), `h_WalPbIn_ZeroLaw` (9), `h_proto_UnmarshalWalRecordE` (5).

`#print axioms` on a result is its trust base (`etc/tcb-report.py`).
-/
